Track 1: Shift-Change at Nine
- Story & Context: The track records the night Marcus Vance missed his final factory clock-out after finding a hidden service door in the Galleria basement, leading him straight into the first unauthorized Low-Valve session. Over an excruciating ten-minute progressive build of low trombone hums and rolling snare cuts, the track captures the exact moment the illegal sound system tapped into the grid power. The breakdown strips back to raw acoustic brass before collapsing into an avalanche of 165 BPM chopped breaks, capturing the panic and thrill of stepping outside the clock. Vance recalls looking at the wall and thinking, "The punch card didn't stamp, but the floor won't stop moving."
